.TH GIT-GUM-COMMIT 1
.SH NAME
git-gum-commit \- create an interactive Conventional Commit with a detailed description
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git gum-commit
.SH DESCRIPTION
This interactive command creates a commit message with an optional detailed,
multi-line description. The message format is based on the Conventional
Commits specification:
.UR https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/#summary
.UE
.PP
The command prompts for the following information:
.TP
.I type
The type of change being committed, such as
.BR fix ,
.BR feat ,
.BR docs ,
or
.BR revert .
.TP
.I scope
An optional value identifying the part of the project being modified.
.TP
.I "short description"
A concise, single-line summary of the change.
.TP
.I "detailed description"
An optional multi-line explanation of the change. Insert a line break by
pressing
.BR Ctrl+J .
.PP
After the information has been entered, the complete commit message is
displayed for review. The command asks for confirmation before creating the
commit.
.PP
If the repository has a configured remote, the command also offers to push the
new commit to it.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
This command requires
.B gum
to be installed. For installation instructions and additional information,
visit:
.UR https://github.com/charmbracelet/gum
.UE
.PP
On macOS,
.B gum
can be installed using Homebrew:
.RS
.nf
brew install gum
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a Conventional Commit:
.RS
.nf
git gum-commit
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-commit (1),
.BR git-push (1)
